Usage: agent-deck connect [assistant] [options]

Connect an assistant bot to agent-deck with one scoped token. Prints one
copy-paste block: the config for that assistant and a short guide it keeps.
Read-only by default; send, approve and launch are opt-in.

Assistants (optional; without one you get a generic block the assistant adapts):
  any        Any assistant (it sets itself up)
  hermes     Hermes Agent
  openclaw   OpenClaw
  grok       Grok (xAI API, remote MCP)
  claude     Claude Code / Claude Desktop
  chatgpt    ChatGPT (via Codex CLI or the Responses API)
  codex      Codex CLI
  slack      Slack bot (HTTP API)
  telegram   Telegram bot (HTTP API)
  mcp        Any MCP client (generic)
  http       Any HTTP client (generic)

Options:
  --scopes LIST   Comma-separated: read,send,approve,launch (default read)
  --name NAME     Token name (default: the assistant). Reusing a name rotates its token
  --url URL       agent-deck web address for HTTP snippets (default http://127.0.0.1:8420)
  --json          Print the connection as JSON (token, config, guide)

Commands:
  connect list [--json]                  List connected assistants and their scopes
  connect revoke <name>                  Revoke a token (effective on its next call)
  connect audit [--name N] [-n 50] [--json]  Show recent assistant calls
  connect serve [--token-file F]         MCP server over stdio (token from F or $AGENTDECK_ASSISTANT_TOKEN)
  connect test [--token-file F] [--name N] [--url U]  Check a token end to end (list_sessions)

Tools: whoami, list_sessions, session_status, read_output (read), send_message (send),
approve (approve), launch_session (launch). There is no stop/remove/restart tool.
Over HTTP (agent-deck web): POST /mcp and /api/assistant/v1/..., bearer token only.
Rate limits per token: 120 read and 10 write calls per minute. Audit log:
assistants-audit.jsonl in the agent-deck data directory (never message bodies).

Examples:
  agent-deck connect                         # generic block, read-only
  agent-deck connect hermes                  # Hermes config + guide
  agent-deck connect claude --scopes read,send
  agent-deck connect telegram --url https://deck.example.ts.net --json
  agent-deck connect revoke hermes
